<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Lights showers seen over parts of S.Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Lights showers seen over parts of S.Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-08-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department forecast light showers at several places in the Central, Sabaragamuwa and Western provinces and Galle and Matara districts for Monday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement on Sunday that gusts of fairly strong winds will continue to prevail along the western slopes of the central hills and elsewhere during showers on Monday.</p>
<p>It released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Sunday morning:</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Canyon		   10.4</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	     9.0</p>
<p>    Kotmale		   2.8</p>
<p>    Laxapana		  7.2</p>
<p>    Moussakele		2.5</p>
<p>    Norton		    9.0</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    0</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   0</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  0</p>
</text>
